You are the INDEPENDENT CHECKER for backend PR #921 (wilplus/backend-cursor), ROUND 2. Supabase/Postgres 15. Merging a migration RUNS it in production on the next deploy. Be skeptical; judge only the text below; say what you could not check. Comment lines, table COMMENT statements, blank lines and half the indentation were stripped to keep this short; nothing else was.

CONTEXT. Under enforce mode every provider call (Whisper etc.) needs a database permit. A training-corpus import (v2_sessions.source='training_import', created by a coach through the import route) has no person's consent receipt, so the founder recorded ONE corpus processing basis (decision N58, agreed with counsel; whether it is legally sufficient is NOT in scope). This migration adds that basis and a separate permit path for imports only, and makes the existing Phase-1 permit writer refuse imports.

ROUND 1 (HO-13). Your paste was cut off inside issue_phase1_provider_permit_v1, so you could not see the end of the file (grants, COMMIT). You raised four points; what changed:
1. Basis selection / future retirement -> retirement is now immediate (trigger requires retired_at <= now()); a unique partial index allows ONE basis in force per source; registration picks that one (covers_source='training_import' AND retired_at IS NULL); permits require the registration's basis to be in force.
2. Idempotency -> session, recording, provider and an object manifest are all required; a replayed key returns its permit only if session, recording, provider, operation, manifest and basis are all IS NOT DISTINCT FROM the original, else IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.
3. Event/state machine -> one call per permit: started (only on issued, unexpired, not yet started) then completed->used or failed->failed (only after started, once); cancelled only before start (sets revoked_at); deleted/delete_failed only after the call ended. Row lock (FOR UPDATE). CHECKs tie status to revoked_at/finished_at; status 'expired'/'revoked' removed (expiry is expires_at).
4. Write protection -> it was at the end of the file you could not see (REVOKE from PUBLIC/anon/authenticated; service_role gets EXECUTE on the three writers and SELECT only). Added: the operations ledger can never be updated/deleted/truncated and a permit can never be deleted/truncated (triggers).
Every caller in the app issues a fresh permit (UUID in the idempotency key) per provider call and records started then completed|failed, so the stricter order changes no live path.

